From be37adeec9737540237176d289ef485e4603c111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "UEI 6.18 port" <vinayak.kulkarni@ametek.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:46:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phy: zynqmp: keep psu_init lane ref clock selection (6.6
 behaviour)

Linux 6.6 left L0_Ln_REF_CLK_SEL untouched when a lane used its own
reference clock. Commit 687d6bccb282 ("phy: zynqmp: Enable reference
clock correctly") now forces the local clock mux in that case.

On UEI ZynqMP boards psu_init routes the 27 MHz DP reference clock from
refclk pin 2 to lane 3 (L0_L3_REF_CLK_SEL = 0x04). Forcing the local mux
feeds the DP PLL the wrong reference and DisplayPort link training fails
("failed to train the DP link"). Restore the 6.6 behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Vinayak Kulkarni <vinayak.kulkarni@ametek.com>
---
 drivers/phy/xilinx/phy-zynqmp.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/xilinx/phy-zynqmp.c b/drivers/phy/xilinx/phy-zynqmp.c
index 087fe402e4e2..5b422275053f 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/xilinx/phy-zynqmp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/xilinx/phy-zynqmp.c
@@ -435,11 +435,14 @@ static int xpsgtr_configure_pll(struct xpsgtr_phy *gtr_phy)
 	xpsgtr_clr_set(gtr_phy->dev, PLL_REF_SEL(gtr_phy->lane),
 		       PLL_FREQ_MASK, ssc->pll_ref_clk);
 
-	/* Enable lane clock sharing, if required */
-	if (gtr_phy->refclk == gtr_phy->lane)
-		xpsgtr_clr_set(gtr_phy->dev, L0_Ln_REF_CLK_SEL(gtr_phy->lane),
-			       L0_REF_CLK_SEL_MASK, L0_REF_CLK_LCL_SEL);
-	else
+	/*
+	 * Enable lane clock sharing, if required. When the lane uses its own
+	 * reference clock, keep the selection programmed by psu_init (FSBL),
+	 * as Linux 6.6 did. Boards may route a reference clock pin to another
+	 * lane in hardware (e.g. UEI: refclk pin 2 -> lane 3 for DP), and
+	 * forcing the local mux breaks the PLL reference.
+	 */
+	if (gtr_phy->refclk != gtr_phy->lane)
 		xpsgtr_clr_set(gtr_phy->dev, L0_Ln_REF_CLK_SEL(gtr_phy->lane),
 			       L0_REF_CLK_SEL_MASK, 1 << gtr_phy->refclk);
 
